@startuml client_server_async_integration

skinparam sequenceArrowColor Black
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor White
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor DarkGray
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor LightYellow
skinparam NoteBorderColor Gray
skinparam NoteTextAlignment left

title Client / Server Integration Pilot: Setup and Asynchronous Request/Reply

actor "Client Application" as ExternalClient <<external>>
participant "client : IClientConnection" as client_api
participant "server : IServer" as server_api
participant "connection : IServerConnection" as server_connection_api
actor "Server Application" as ExternalServer <<external>>

note across : OS-independent public API view; IPC arrows are transport messages, not C++ method calls.\nClient/server objects have been created through IClientFactory/IServerFactory with matching protocol configuration.\nOne permitted interleaving is shown; callback completion is not guaranteed to happen after an API call returns.

note over ExternalClient, client_api : Pilot configuration: sync_first_connect = false, truly_async = true,\nmax_async_replies >= 1, max_queued_sends >= 1; one request, non-empty callbacks.
note over server_api, ExternalServer : This pilot uses UserData containing a context pointer.\nReturning a unique_ptr<IConnectionHandler> instead selects its methods\nin place of the non-connect server callbacks; that alternative is not shown.

== Register server callbacks ==

ExternalServer -> server_api : StartListening(connect_callback, disconnect_callback,\nsent_callback, sent_with_reply_callback)
server_api --> ExternalServer : expected_blank<Error>{} (listening)

== Register client callbacks and start ==

ExternalClient -> client_api : Start(state_callback, notify_callback)
activate client_api
client_api -> ExternalClient : state_callback(State::kStarting)
note over ExternalClient, client_api : Nested in Start(), on the calling thread.\nThe callback may call Stop(); this scenario continues without stopping.
ExternalClient --> client_api : void
client_api --> ExternalClient : void
deactivate client_api

== Accept a connection ==

client_api ->> server_api : IPC: connection attempt
server_api -> ExternalServer : connect_callback(connection)
ExternalServer --> server_api : expected<UserData, Error>{context_ptr}
note over server_connection_api, ExternalServer : The library owns connection; the callback receives an IServerConnection&.\nUserData is associated with the accepted connection, not returned to the client.
server_api -->> client_api : IPC: connection accepted
client_api -> ExternalClient : state_callback(State::kReady)
ExternalClient --> client_api : void
note over ExternalClient, client_api : Ready follows return from the Starting callback.\nReady's thread is unspecified; it may precede return from Start().

== Submit an asynchronous request ==

ExternalClient -> client_api : SendWithCallback(message, reply_callback)
alt Local rejection: message exceeds max_send_size
    client_api --> ExternalClient : unexpected(EMSGSIZE)
    note over ExternalClient, client_api : No request accepted and no reply_callback invocation for this call.
else Request accepted for background transmission
    client_api --> ExternalClient : expected_blank<Error>{}
    note over ExternalClient, client_api : Success means accepted, not delivered or replied to.\nReturning before completion is the interleaving shown, not a guarantee.

    alt Request and reply delivered successfully
        client_api ->> server_connection_api : IPC: request(message)
        server_connection_api -> ExternalServer : sent_with_reply_callback(connection, message)
        activate ExternalServer
        ExternalServer -> server_connection_api : Reply(reply)
        server_connection_api --> ExternalServer : expected_blank<Error>{}
        ExternalServer --> server_connection_api : expected_blank<Error>{}
        deactivate ExternalServer
        note over server_connection_api, ExternalServer : Returning success from sent_with_reply_callback does not send a reply.\nReply() is a separate call on connection, shown inside the callback here.\nA valid-size reply and successful delivery are assumed in this branch.

        server_connection_api -->> client_api : IPC: reply(reply)
        client_api -> ExternalClient : reply_callback(expected<span<const uint8_t>, Error>{reply})
        ExternalClient --> client_api : void
    else Background send fails or peer disconnects before a reply
        client_api -> ExternalClient : reply_callback(unexpected(Error))
        ExternalClient --> client_api : void
        note over ExternalClient, client_api : Error is reported by reply_callback, not by the earlier successful return.\nConnection loss also produces Stopping/Stopped state callbacks (not expanded here);\na background send failure need not stop the connection.
    end
end

note over ExternalClient, client_api : Client callback threads are unspecified except where stated.\nStart() callback captures must remain alive until kStopped;\nreply_callback captures must survive completion. Teardown is not shown.
note over server_api, ExternalServer : Server callbacks for one session are serialized; their threads are unspecified.\nServer-callback captures must remain alive until StopListening() returns.\nStopListening() must not be called from a server callback.

@enduml